              "description": "Upper secant and lower tangent from external E, retaining the internal 5 and external x labels.",
              "mathematics": "Internal secant segment 5, external segment x, tangent AE=6; x(x+5)=36.",
              "answerVisibility": "The corrected solution is not included in the question figure."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=4$",
          "worked": "By the tangent–secant form of the Power of a Point Theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+5)&=6^2\\\\x^2+5x&=36\\\\x^2+5x-36&=0\\\\(x+9)(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $x=-9$ since a length is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
